  "articleBody": "Picking the right contractor for your general home repairs can feel a bit like dating – you want someone reliable, experienced, and who communicates well! First, look for a contractor with solid experience in projects similar to yours. Don't be shy about asking for references and actually checking them. It's a huge red flag if they can't provide any. Next, make sure they're insured and licensed, especially for larger jobs or anything needing permits. This protects you if anything goes wrong. Always get a written scope of work and an itemized estimate, so you know exactly what you’re paying for and what’s included. HH Remodeling LLC, a BBB Accredited Business, is known for transparent communication and detailed plans. You want a contractor who’s clear about start and end dates and how they’ll handle unexpected delays. Finally, make sure they offer a warranty on their labor and materials. This shows they stand behind their work. If you're dealing with anything complex like potential structural issues or extensive damage, a qualified professional's expertise is invaluable for ensuring a safe and durable repair.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}